  "claim": {
    "statement": "L3 (M.51 K3 + M.52 L3) is EMPIRICALLY REFINED by M.54: although the three inquiry systems have non-overlapping architectural inputs/outputs/cadence (verified in M.51/M.52), they nonetheless CONVERGE on the same events at the empirical level. Specifically, 2 statistical signal(s) survive Bonferroni correction across 5 tests (\u03b1 = 0.01000). This is detection-by-coincidence-of-physics, not by design: the underlying substrate signals (text density, semantic regularity) trigger both Walker M3 oscillator-physics and Zetetic concept-pair detection naturally. The architectural gap remains real; the empirical redundancy is informative.",
    "operationalization": "100 Shakespeare paragraphs from pg100.txt run through fresh Takwin. Per cycle: capture resolution (Walker M3-proxy via halt mode), n_zetetic_contradictions (Zetetic System 2 intensity), walk_length, phi. Statistical tests: Mann-Whitney U on zetetic-intensity between halt modes (3 pairs), Spearman rank correlation zetetic-vs-walk-length, Spearman zetetic-vs-phi. Bonferroni correction across all tests.",
    "threshold": {
      "metric": "n_convergence_signals_surviving_bonferroni",
      "comparator": ">=",
      "value": 1.0,
      "units": "tests"
    },
    "h0": "Inquiry systems are statistically independent across reasoning events",
    "h1": "Inquiry systems converge on the same events without architectural coupling"
  },
